       "k": "h",
       "label": "h",
       "min": 0.001,
       "max": 1,
       "step": 0.001,
       "v": 0.5
      }
     ],
     "formula": "((1 + h) ** 3 - 1) / h",
     "out": "Average rate = {v}",
     "note": "At h = 0.1 it is 3.31. Near h = 0 it is 3.",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-1-1.20"
    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "Instantaneous rate of change",
     "paras": [
      "It is the change at one particular moment.",
      "Use (f(x₀ + h) − f(x₀))/h and let h get closer and closer to 0."
     ],
     "note": "Average rate: over an interval. Instantaneous rate: at one point.",
     "ref": "Definition 2.3",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-1-1.21"
    },
    {
     "kind": "name",
     "step": "name",
     "title": "Key words",
     "defs": [
      [
       "Instantaneous rate of change",
       "The value (f(x₀ + h) − f(x₀))/h approaches as h gets closer to 0."
      ]
     ],
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-1-1.22"
    },
    {
     "kind": "steps",
     "step": "method",
     "title": "f(x) = 2x² + 9 at x = −3",
     "steps": [
      "f(−3 + h) = 2(h² − 6h + 9) + 9 = 2h² − 12h + 27.",
      "f(−3) = 2(9) + 9 = 27.",
      "Difference: 2h² − 12h. Divide by h: 2h − 12.",
      "As h → 0, 2h − 12 → −12."
     ],
     "ref": "Example 1",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-1-1.23"
    },
    {
